WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:04.004
Alright here it comes, 
and 3,2,1, action!

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:07.382
♪♪

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:11.011
They created this whole
crazy epic world.

00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:14.264
This season everyone is
changing and evolving.

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:15.766
It’s just real exciting.

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:17.434
I think people are going to be
blown away,

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.186
when they see what
season two looks like.

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:25.943
Boom, uggghhhh, love my job.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.783
With season two it’s amazing
what we’ve pulled off.

00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:37.204
It’s not an easy thing to create
these huge epic worlds.

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:39.540
These civilizations.
These kingdoms.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.668
Let us not wait until they knock
down our gates.

00:00:42.668 --> 00:00:45.462
I say we open it right now

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:48.382
and protect what is ours
at all costs.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.843
For season two we wanted to come
down off the mountains

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:54.429
and see what life was like in
what used to be the cities.

00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:57.933
Leaving season one and coming
into a city and seeing its decay

00:00:57.933 --> 00:01:00.477
after six hundred years, it’s a
whole different look,

00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:02.145
you know, he’s crawling
back into Hell.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:07.276
We are moving along
geographically and we come to

00:01:07.276 --> 00:01:10.862
places that would be cities,
in the aftermath,

00:01:10.862 --> 00:01:13.573
all those hundreds
of years in the future.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:14.908
How cold is it J?

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:18.954
It’s negative 20.
(laughs)

00:01:18.954 --> 00:01:20.330
I like the cold. I don’t know,

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.874
I always end up in the cold
or in water.

00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:24.668
We took that destroyed

00:01:24.668 --> 00:01:26.586
city aesthetic and really
ran with it.

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:30.299
Just the expanse of it
is pretty spectacular.

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:33.343
The main streetwhere we’ve
turned cars on their end and

00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:36.096
stacked them to be the wall and

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:39.725
then we used quite literally
a bus as the gate.

00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:41.393
It was quite a sight actually.

00:01:49.735 --> 00:01:51.862
We always want to kinda make the
scope and scale and

00:01:51.862 --> 00:01:55.449
The Hearn allowed that because
of the geography of this coal

00:01:55.449 --> 00:01:57.451
fired plant that’s just massive.

00:01:58.285 --> 00:02:01.330
This is one of the coolest sets
I’ve ever been on in my life.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:06.126
Look at that. Look over there.
It’s amazing.

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:08.712
I’ve never been in a
building that big.

00:02:08.712 --> 00:02:11.590
There are some shots in there
that are just like unbelievable.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.935
Awesome.

00:02:23.935 --> 00:02:25.979
I just got drooled
on by Bautista.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:29.149
Awesome. Awesome. Awesome.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.527
A lot of the things we build are
beautiful,

00:02:32.527 --> 00:02:34.529
but there is also a
lot of logic built into it.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:37.437
We have a full crew of artists
who build everything for the

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:42.204
show in house, which is really
unique for television.

00:02:43.205 --> 00:02:48.877
I just love that we can put
things in there that we know

00:02:45.916 --> 00:02:48.168
from our time and they have
become something else.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.878
I think that’s brilliant.

00:02:49.878 --> 00:02:52.005
It forces you to think outside
the box and use your other

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:55.008
senses for fabrics, by touch
it is the texture,

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:59.262
and then also does
it make sound.

00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:00.514
My queen.

00:03:02.224 --> 00:03:05.227
This is basically me being a six
year old boy. Dream come true.

00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:10.440
Best, best outfit ever.
I’m going to be a samurai.

00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:13.860
Jason would be the
quintessential warrior.

00:03:13.902 --> 00:03:14.903
In all factions.

00:03:17.948 --> 00:03:20.534
My love for Japanese culture
happen to coincide with

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:23.036
Jason’s love for
Japanese culture

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.372
and he always wanted to have
this kind of influence

00:03:25.372 --> 00:03:27.249
and so I thought,
hey let’s do samurai.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:30.544
My whole life I wanted to play a
samurai.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.838
I love Yojimbo and Seven Samurai

00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:35.590
and so I always wanted to play a
character like that.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.970
When you see him emerge in that,
along with the robes,

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:44.683
the kimono and the hakama.
He looks powerful.

00:03:44.683 --> 00:03:53.150
(Inaudible) Dream job.

00:03:54.317 --> 00:04:00.574
I had all of these made for me.
Look at that. Woo!

00:04:00.574 --> 00:04:02.033
Jason loves his weapons.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.077
Yeah!

00:04:04.202 --> 00:04:06.580
I had a dream of different
things I wanted to make.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.248
Picked out the antlers I wanted,

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:10.834
picked out the style of knife
that I wanted.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:11.960
Finally it’s here.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:15.589
Woah! Look at that!

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.341
These swords were made in
Hawaii.

00:04:18.341 --> 00:04:20.093
The rest pretty much in Texas.

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:22.929
That is perfect.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:27.726
Everything from the weapons to
the costume department to the

00:04:27.726 --> 00:04:31.062
sets department. Everyone really
wants to elevate this season.

00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:34.649
There’s too many of them.

00:04:34.733 --> 00:04:36.735
Advance!

00:04:37.819 --> 00:04:40.280
In the world of See you can be
the Queen.

00:04:40.989 --> 00:04:42.782
You can be a leader of a tribe.

00:04:44.159 --> 00:04:45.410
You can be a warrior.

00:04:46.161 --> 00:04:48.788
Each individual is treated as
an equal in our show.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:52.292
Look at this. 
This is why I love movies.

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:56.630
All these beautiful people,
that make it possible.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.466
I get to travel the world, and
meet all types of artists,

00:04:59.466 --> 00:05:01.426
that get to build
worlds like this.

00:05:01.426 --> 00:05:05.347
We all come together to make
something that hopefully changes

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:08.058
your perspective and be

00:05:08.058 --> 00:05:10.060
compassionate to
other people’s lives.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.895
I love it.

00:05:12.896 --> 00:05:14.064
Baba!

00:05:14.105 --> 00:05:15.941
Now!

00:05:21.029 --> 00:05:23.365
The level of ambition on this
show is through the roof.

00:05:24.115 --> 00:05:27.160
This whole season has been
incredible.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.206
I am a father.

00:05:32.082 --> 00:05:34.042
I am a husband.

00:05:34.042 --> 00:05:35.418
I am your friend.

00:05:35.794 --> 00:05:37.963
I am Baba Voss

00:05:37.963 --> 00:05:40.340
and I am fighting for your
freedom

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.342
until the day that I die.

00:05:48.932 --> 00:05:49.599
Boom.

